"Path.Merge fails silently when database operations succeed"
"The Path.Merge method has incorrect error handling logic that causes it to return errors when database operations succeed, rather than when they fail."
"the method returns an error when `err == nil` (success) instead of when `err != nil` (failure)."

This is really confusing. If database operations succeed (`err == nil`), then the method should return `nil`, not an error.

Unless... unless there's supposed to be some validation that should cause an error when operations succeed, which would be very unusual.

